	(text "ORANGE PI 5 LINK. The board is a HAT on the Orange Pi 5: four M2.5 x 20 mm standoffs (the Pi's\nUSB/Ethernet stack is 16.2 mm tall) and J41, a 2x9 female socket under the board on the Pi's pins 1-18.\nThe UART and reset cross U8 and U9, so the Pi's ground (GND_PI) never meets this board's ground:\nmotor and LED return current cannot flow through the Pi, and a fault on the 24 V side stops at the barrier.\nThe Pi powers its side (pin 1, 3.3 V). Keep GND_PI copper 1 mm or more from GND.\nFirmware: PIO UART, GP7 TX, GP19 RX. Pi: enable the uart0-m2 overlay (/dev/ttyS0); drive pin 15 (GPIO0_D4) high to reset the Pico."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3657bba1-cacb-45a1-b630-a71c48966847")
	)
